Problem Description:
Find the bug and fix this 8-bit wide 2-to-1 mux.

// module top_module (
//     input sel,
//     input [7:0] a,
//     input [7:0] b,
//     output out  );

//     assign out = (~sel & a) | (sel & b);

// endmodule

module top_module (
	input sel,
	input [7:0] a,
	input [7:0] b,
	output reg [7:0] out
);

Erroneous Implementation:

always @(posedge clk)
begin
	if (sel == 0)
	begin
		out <= b;
	end
	else
	begin
		out <= a;
	end
end

endmodule

Feedback:
bugs_mux2.sv:163: error: Unable to bind wire/reg/memory `clk' in `tb.top_module1'
bugs_mux2.sv:163: error: Failed to evaluate event expression 'posedge clk'.
2 error(s) during elaboration.

```verilog
module top_module (
    input sel,
    input [7:0] a,
    input [7:0] b,
    output [7:0] out
);

    // A 2-to-1 mux is a combinational circuit.
    // The error in the original code was:
    // 1. Using a 'clk' signal that was not defined in the input ports.
    // 2. Implementing the mux as sequential logic (always @(posedge clk)) instead of combinational.
    // 3. The logic was inverted (sel=0 should select 'a', but the code selected 'b').

    assign out = sel ? b : a;

endmodule
```
